  "body": "I have an Accordion menu where each section is toggled by clicking the header of the panel. The entire header is a `button` element.\r\n\r\nThe header contains a value that you can set in the content of the panel. It also contains an element that you can click to reset the value. This is also an interactive element that I expect to make a `button`. Clicking it should not open or close the panel. \r\n\r\nI expect this to be valid HTML:\r\n\r\n```\r\n<div class=\"accordion\">\r\n  <div class=\"accordion-panel\">\r\n    <button class=\"accordion-panel-header\" type=\"button\">\r\n      From: 2015-05-01\r\n      <button type=\"button\">(reset)</button>\r\n    </button>\r\n    <div class=\"accordion-panel-body\">date picker</div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>\r\n```\r\n\r\nI realize I could perhaps use `details`/`summary` for this particular example, but I still consider it a valid use case.",
